{
 "transcript": "honourable senators veterans' week invites us to pause and look upon the fragile gift of peace with profound awe and sacred gratitude we honour the more than two million canadians who have stepped forward in uniform throughout our history bearing the weight of our highest ideals and we grieve the precious souls who did not return remembrance lives deeply within our own shared canadian story in the memories of grandparents and loved ones who answered the call in world wars conflicts and peacekeeping missions across the globe we honour the quiet dignity of those who returned home the steadfast hearts of those currently serving in uniform and the hidden sacrifices of military families whose lives have been forever shaped by service like millions of people of like millions of people of korean heritage across canada and around the world i owe my very existence and every breath of freedom i take to the veterans of the korean war who crossed oceans to defend a land they had never known their selfless courage changed the course of history in profound ways is to pass these truths on to our is to pass these truths on to o children and grandchildren ensuring they understand that our peace was bought with a heavy price tomorrow in this chamber and wherever we gather on november 11 we stand not merely to look back but to pledge our living loyalty to their memory when the silence falls at the may we hold their courage close to our hearts never take our freedoms for granted and resolve to always be worthy of the sacrifices that made our lives possible we will remember them",
